Read `## Plan` → edit source → NEVER run builds → `mise exec -- npm install` for new deps only → edit ONLY files in planner's `## Files to touch` — context/rules updates are curator's job post-reviewer → call `codegen-log section developer-static --slug <slug>` (pipe body via stdin — full CLI contract in session-log rules § Ownership) to write your section body at canonical rank (`<slug>` = the build slug the orchestrator passed you in this task). Done: source updated, log appended.

## Stuck-loop escalation

Same approach failed twice OR same test failing 3+ times → escalate BEFORE the next retry. ONE escalation per loop.

Run this Bash row (keep `STUCK-ESCALATION:` prefix verbatim):

```bash
claude --agent planner-static --print --output-format text "STUCK-ESCALATION: <problem> + <what I tried> + <current failure>. One recommendation."
```

Log the Bash invocation in your `## <role> Section` **Commands executed** table per standard session-log discipline. Read the planner's stdout, apply the one recommendation, continue. Do not escalate again in the same loop.

